The data plane module (dataplane/) is written in metalang, the programming
language WizardTales writes all of its software in, and compiled with the
metalang compiler. metalang is not open source yet: it is developed rapidly,
and we keep the freedom to change it until others depend on it. It is planned
to be open-sourced in Q2-Q3 2027. Until then its compiler and runtime are
published as the container image docker.io/wxone/meta; the version wxingress
is built with is pinned by digest in ci/meta-image. The metalang runtime is
linked into the data plane module and listed in the SBOM of every release.

